# 🔟 Partition Labels

## 📖 Problem

Partition a string into maximum parts so that each letter appears in only one part.

---

### Example

```text
ababcbacadefegdehijhklij
```

Output:

```text
9 7 8
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Greedy Strategy

First find:

```text
Last occurrence
```

of every character.

While traversing:

```text
Keep extending partition
```

until current index reaches the farthest last occurrence.

Then cut the partition.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> partitionLabels(
    string s)
{
    vector<int> last(
        26,
        0
    );

    for(int i = 0;
        i < s.size();
        i++)
    {
        last[s[i]-'a'] = i;
    }

    vector<int> answer;

    int start = 0;
    int end = 0;

    for(int i = 0;
        i < s.size();
        i++)
    {
        end =
            max(
                end,
                last[s[i]-'a']
            );

        if(i == end)
        {
            answer.push_back(
                end - start + 1
            );

            start = i + 1;
        }
    }

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(1)
```

